/akili-validate design gate - detector evidence, 2026-11-20, HEAD 2380642ca0, engine impeccable-engine 0.1.18 (vendored skill 4.8.0).
App: throwaway git worktree of HEAD outside the repo, run with scripts/run-marlo-java17.sh, DB aiccradb_partreq_test (copy). <skill-dir> = the global impeccable skill folder.

## 1. Source scan (one pass, pattern rules only)
IMPECCABLE_BIN=<skill-dir>/scripts/bin/darwin-arm64/impeccable DO_NOT_TRACK=1 IMPECCABLE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 <skill-dir>/scripts/impeccable detect --json <9 files: superadmin/marloInstitutions.ftl, institutionRequestMacro.ftl, rejectInstitutionPopup.ftl, allInstitutionsPopup.ftl, partnersSave.ftl, marloInstitutions.css, partnersSave.css, marloInstitutions.js, partnersSave.js>
exit=0, findings=0 ([]). The engine states that .ftl/.css are scanned with regex rules only (element rules like tiny-text, low-contrast do not run on source).
Positive control (scratch file, not in repo): a .ftl with gradient text gave exit=2, 1 gradient-text finding, so .ftl files are read.

## 2. URL scans (authenticated)
The detector takes no cookie/header, so the authenticated page was reached with --cdp: a headless Chrome on a local DevTools port, fresh profile per capture (no stored consent),
superadmin session cookie set through playwright-cli attach (cookie obtained by a login POST; never printed). Viewport set by Playwright device-metrics emulation; a separate CDP session read
innerWidth x innerHeight = the requested viewport during and after every scan (poll during one scan: 8/8 reads 390x844).
Command: IMPECCABLE_BIN=<skill-dir>/scripts/bin/darwin-arm64/impeccable DO_NOT_TRACK=1 IMPECCABLE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 <skill-dir>/scripts/impeccable detect --json --cdp <port> --target <page path> [--no-consent-hiding --no-overlay-hiding]
Viewports: desktop 1280x800, mobile 390x844 (defaults: docs/ux-ui/design.md §9 declares none). Every non-2 exit stderr: none (all exits 2; stderr empty).

